<title>UK: John Lewis 1996 pre-tax profit leaps.</title>
<headline>John Lewis 1996 pre-tax profit leaps.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 months to</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p>Pretax before</p>
<p> partnership bonus	217		    vs 150</p>
<p> Pretax		     135.3		  vs 93</p>
<p> Turnover		   2,850		  vs 2,541</p>
<p> Trading profit	   238.8		  vs 172.8</p>
<p>John Lewis Partnership Plc operates 23 department stores and 115 Waitrose supermarkets across Britain and said its record bonus of 82 million stg, to be shared among its employees, was at a rate of about 20 percent -- or about 10 weeks' pay each.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44-171 5452 7717</p>
</text>
